2026-09-23: repeated logical-negation regression, GNU11 AArch64.
RED: optimized normalize(int n) { return !!!!n; } emitted five integer
comparisons instead of one. This was redundant work, not a wrong value.
GREEN: one comparison; the native function shrank from 28 to 8 instructions.
C-HIR, optimized and unoptimized EvoIR, GCC14, Clang19 and EvoCC native
execute logical-normalization.c with result 0. Calls, postincrement,
short-circuit assignment, pointer, 128-bit and FP truth cases are included.
Separate optimized/unoptimized negative tests retain E3001 for an
uninitialized operand and E3009 for a null dereference.
The changed gate passed 1078 tests, with 3 existing ignored tests, and
Clippy -D warnings and fmt passed. No kernel timeout or crash is closed
by this isolated measurement.
